            <title>[LU-21334]  mount.lustre default md_stripe_cache_size=16384 uses too much memory</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21334</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;mount.lustre sets mo_md_stripe_cache_size to 16384 by default&lt;br/&gt;
(set_defaults() in lustre/utils/mount_lustre.c).  At each OST mount,&lt;br/&gt;
tune_md_stripe_cache_size() in libmount_utils_ldiskfs.c writes this value&lt;br/&gt;
to /sys/block/mdN/md/stripe_cache_size when the current value is lower.&lt;br/&gt;
It never lowers it.  So every md device under an OST gets 16384 stripe&lt;br/&gt;
heads unless the operator sets the mount option.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Each stripe head holds one page per member device, plus about 1.8 KiB:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;cost = stripe_cache_size * (members * PAGE_SIZE + head)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;4-member array: about 285 MiB&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;10-member array: about 670 MiB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;This is per array, and the md shrinker does not go below the value that&lt;br/&gt;
was set.  On a 2 GiB server with 4 arrays the stripe caches used 1.14 GiB,&lt;br/&gt;
then other allocations failed ("page allocation failure: order:4" from&lt;br/&gt;
mount.lustre, netlink ENOBUFS).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The man page also says the unit is KiB; it is a count of stripe heads.&lt;br/&gt;
It says MDT devices are tuned, but tune_block_dev() returns early for&lt;br/&gt;
anything that is not an OST.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Proposed fix: default to 0, so mount.lustre leaves the device's own value&lt;br/&gt;
alone.  -o md_stripe_cache_size=&amp;lt;num&amp;gt; works as before.  Document the&lt;br/&gt;
sizing rule for md RAID5/6 over HDDs, where a small cache costs write&lt;br/&gt;
throughput (a 10-member RAID6 with 8 writers of 4 MiB lost 52% at 256&lt;br/&gt;
compared with 16384).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproducer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Create an md RAID5/6 device with 4 members.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;cat /sys/block/mdN/md/stripe_cache_size (for example 256).&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;mkfs.lustre --ost ... /dev/mdN; mount -t lustre /dev/mdN /mnt/ost&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;cat /sys/block/mdN/md/stripe_cache_size again: it is now 16384.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</description>
